# General rules

## Comment style

Never use block comments of the form `/** ... */` or `/* ... */`.

Always use line comments with `//`.

```typescript
// BAD
/** Stores a memory fact. */
export function remember() {}

/* multi-line
   block comment */

// GOOD
// Stores a memory fact.
export function remember() {}

// Multi-line comments use
// consecutive // lines.
```

This applies to TypeScript, JavaScript, and similar languages in this repo.

## Development tasks

Before creating, editing, or closing a task or epic under `docs/tasks/`, read
and follow [task-writing.mdc](./task-writing.mdc).

Create and close documents only with `scripts/task.py`. Run from the repository
root, changing into the tracker directory in the same command:

- `cd docs/tasks && python3 ../../scripts/task.py create`
- `cd docs/tasks && python3 ../../scripts/task.py create --epic`
- `cd docs/tasks && python3 ../../scripts/task.py close TASK-001`
- `cd docs/tasks && python3 ../../scripts/task.py close EPIC-001`

Never allocate numbers or move documents into archives by hand. Closed tasks
and epics are immutable historical records; only `scripts/task.py` may update
their links. Do not rewrite them to match later code.
